      "content": "Working: Fibonacci Series Using Memoization"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here's how the previous code works:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "1. The map fib is initialized with the base cases."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "// Fibonacci(0) = 0\n// Fibonacci(1) = 1\nunordered_map<int, int> fib = {{0, 0}, {1, 1}};"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "2. Fibonacci(4) is called."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "When we call Fibonacci(4), it first checks if key 4 is in the fib map."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Since key 4 is not present, its value (fib[4]) is calculated as:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "fib[4] = Fibonacci(3) + Fibonacci(2)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "As a result, Fibonacci(4) ends up calling Fibonacci(3)."
    },
